  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Formation of an acetal occurs&nbsp;when the hydroxyl group of a hemiacetal becomes protonated and is lost as water. The carbocation that is produced is then rapidly attacked by a molecule of alcohol. Loss of the proton from the attached alcohol gives the acetal.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e112117d-0477-4dbf-87ae-ea0358630ccf-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 95px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
